## Vercel Speed Insights Configuration Update

### Summary
Successfully updated Vercel Speed Insights configuration to use the recommended React component approach as per the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

### What Was Changed

#### Modified Files:
1. **src/main.tsx**
   - Removed the deprecated `injectSpeedInsights()` function call
   - Removed the `import { injectSpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights"` statement
   - Cleaned up the file to use the recommended React component approach instead of script injection

2. **src/App.tsx**
   - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react"`
   - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component alongside the existing `<VercelAnalytics />` component
   - Placed the component at the root level of the application for proper tracking across all pages

### Implementation Details

The project already had `@vercel/speed-insights` version `2.0.0` installed in its dependencies. However, it was using the older script injection method (`injectSpeedInsights()`). 

According to the latest Vercel documentation:
- The React component approach (`<SpeedInsights />`) is the recommended method for React applications
- It offers more seamless integration with React frameworks
- The component automatically collects Web Vitals and performance metrics when deployed to Vercel

The SpeedInsights component is now:
- Properly imported from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Added at the root level in App.tsx alongside VercelAnalytics
- Will automatically track performance metrics across all routes in the application

### Build Verification
- ✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
- ✅ No TypeScript compilation errors
- ✅ Existing functionality preserved
- ✅ Dependencies already installed (no package.json changes needed)

### Notes
- The implementation follows the Vite + React framework-specific instructions from the official Vercel documentation
- The SpeedInsights component is a wrapper around the tracking script, providing better React integration
- No additional configuration is required; metrics will be automatically collected when deployed to Vercel
- The component is placed in a non-blocking location that won't affect page load performance
